ROUND-116 (probe session, all findings measured):
  * GNIL/RTHROW tagging localized the failure exactly: deduction of
    `__bind_back(_Fn...)` leaves _Fn UNASSIGNED
    (guess_function_template_args' has_unassigned() give-up), then
    resolve's all-templates [temp.deduct]/8 throw fires.  b3 and b4
    BOTH fail deduction -- b3 recovers through a later retry, so the
    b3/b4 split is about RECOVERY, not deduction.
  * ROOT: [dcl.fct]/6 + [temp.variadic]/1 -- `_Fn...` with a non-pack
    _Fn is `_Fn, ...` (one deducible parameter + C VARARGS), not a
    function parameter pack.  CBMC's deduction treats every
    ellipsis-marked declarator as a pack and consumes ALL call
    arguments into _Fn.
  * Attempted fix (reverted): flipping is_pack=false on positive
    identification (bare name matching a non-pack template parameter)
    breaks b3 as well -- with is_pack=false the INSTANTIATED candidate's
    parameter list lacks the `...` varargs marker (code_typet
    has_ellipsis), so a 2-argument call fails arity matching.  The
    complete fix must BOTH deduce _Fn from the first argument only AND
    mark the instantiated code_typet as variadic ([dcl.fct]/6).  That
    signature-side propagation is the open piece.

ROUND-116 (cont.): the two-part varargs fix (deduction-side
is_pack=false + signature-side ellipsis marker on
guess_function_template_args' function_type, marker correctly on the
ID_parameters node) still leaves b2/b3/b4 failing AND regresses b3's
previous recovery -- overload matching runs against the signature the
INSTANTIATION path builds (instantiate_template ->
convert_non_template_declaration), not (only) guess's local
function_type, so the varargs conversion must be implemented THERE as
well (three sites total).  Reverted; the design is sound per
[dcl.fct]/6 but needs the instantiate_template leg.  Both attempts'
diffs preserved in this desc's history via git.

